    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d280">

                <pb facs="0381" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/260</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1458</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 19, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with my despatch No. 1455 of
                    April 14, dealing with the Grand Canal contract, I have the honor to add, in
                    order <pb facs="0382" n="216" xml:id="pg216"/> to avoid misunderstanding, that
                    when my opinion was asked by Chinese officials concerning the advisability of
                    accepting the suggestion of the American International Corporation with respect
                    to giving to Japanese capitalists a share in the financing of the canal
                    enterprise, I have replied in a sense favorable to the suggestion. * * *
                    Unfortunately the further proposal now revealed that there is to be
                    participation not only in the financing, but also in construction and
                    management, will make our position far more difficult.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paul S. Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
